; PC-CMP-02B-BT-ONLY.ERB -- 对拍装置夹具 A2b（ONLY 遮蔽实验）
; Question this case answers: PC registers an #ONLY label in bucket 0 AND bucket 2
;   (reference/emuera-skia-4.981/Emuera/Runtime/Script/Data/LabelDictionary.cs:134-141, first and
;    fourth if), yet nobody ever sees the duplicate. Why?
;   reference/emuera-cs/MinorShift.Emuera.Runtime.Script/ProcessState.cs:326-329
;     if (calledFunction.IsOnly) calledFunction.FinishEvent();
;   FinishEvent (:259-264) sets group = 4 and CurrentLabel = null, so the FIRST return of the
;   #ONLY member ends the whole event dispatch and bucket 2 is never reached.
;   Same tri-branch on the fork: reference/emuera-skia-4.981/Emuera/Runtime/Script/Process.State.cs:505-510.
; So the duplicate registration is REAL but MASKED. The port models it as an exclusive bucket 0
;   (core-vm/.../proc/FuncMeta.kt:227-233) and therefore cannot distinguish "masked duplicate"
;   from "no duplicate" -- which is the argument in the 判词 for why the ONLY half of the fork
;   (FuncMeta.kt:213-226 TODO(verify)) cannot be settled by looking at the bucket list alone.
; Expected on PC 4.981: DRIVER -> nested BEFORE_THROW bucket 0: ONLY, then nothing.
;   PCMARK-BT2-PRI, PCMARK-BT2-N and PCMARK-BT2-THROWN all ABSENT.
; Expected on the port (exclusive): DRIVER -> ONLY, PRI, N (bucket 1 and 2 keep running) -> diff.
; One boot only, see PC-CMP-02A header (pending throw re-fires after BEFORE_THROW finishes).

@EVENTLOAD
#LATER
	PRINTFORML PCMARK-BT2-DRIVER
	THROW PC-CMP-02B
	PRINTFORML PCMARK-BT2-THROWN

@BEFORE_THROW
#ONLY
	PRINTFORML PCMARK-BT2-ONLY

@BEFORE_THROW
#PRI
	PRINTFORML PCMARK-BT2-PRI

@BEFORE_THROW
	PRINTFORML PCMARK-BT2-N
